# extract-ikconfig.SOURCE

`extract-ikconfig` in this directory is a verbatim copy of the Linux kernel's
`scripts/extract-ikconfig`, vendored here so the differential test in
`tests/builder/profile-test.py` needs no network access.

- Upstream source: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/3938c8d97142d5cf31543aa96f864a2cf832dda0/scripts/extract-ikconfig?format=TEXT
- Kernel commit:   3938c8d97142d5cf31543aa96f864a2cf832dda0
- License:         The script header says only "Licensed under the terms of the GNU General Public License."
                   It names no version and has no SPDX tag. The kernel's COPYING applies to files
                   without an SPDX tag (GPL-2.0-only for kernel/common). This copy is a test fixture
                   run as its own process; it is not linked into the image.
                   The full texts, byte-identical to kernel/common 3938c8d97142, are next to this note.
                   Do not edit them. They are not a reconstruction.
                   - kernel-LICENSES-preferred-GPL-2.0 is LICENSES/preferred/GPL-2.0
                     sha256 8780e78a1a737e127f25a65f6d95269bffd36158dc261114de7859b490bfc5aa (18600 bytes)
                   - kernel-COPYING is COPYING
                     sha256 fb5a425bd3b3cd6071a3a9aff9909a859e7c1158d54d32e07658398cd67eb6a0 (496 bytes)
- sha256:          070020a9c5a0b9e6f7e24f5728073e8e62155be49133a9f3f37e8fc19230a9b1
- Size:            1779 bytes

The vendored file is kept byte-identical to upstream so that the pinned
sha256 in `profile-test.py` (`_IKCFG_SHA`) still matches. Do not edit
`extract-ikconfig`; put any local notes here instead.
